        },
        {
          "text": "95",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "FDP-ADD-PERCENT"
        },
        {
          "text": "68",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "FDP-DECREASE-MULT"
        },
        {
          "text": "12",
          "correct": false,
          "catches": "FDP-PERCENT-WHOLE"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "10% of 80 is 8 and 5% is 4, so 15% is 12. Then 80 + 12 = 92. Adding the 15 straight on gives 95, which is not 15% of 80. 68 takes 15% off, and 12 is only the increase, not the new amount."
    },
    {
      "key": "fdp-increase-multiplier",
      "band": 3,
      "archetype": "G",
      "answerType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
      "prompt": "Which multiplier increases an amount by 15%?",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "1.15",
